# [DD-13b.W1.3] COMPOSITION, and the three tiers in one file.
#
# `piece` NAMES and EXPORTS one group (DELIVERED at the site below: a
# groups[] row `d.kept` whose ref is "piece"), references one by number
# (HIDDEN: a slot, no row), and leaves one unnamed and unreferenced (ERASED:
# the A_CAP is deleted and it spends no number at all). The caller declares
# no group of its own, so `ngroups` is 0 and every slot above it belongs to
# the definition or to the site.
#
# [D89 addendum, 2026-09-03] THE CALL IS A DELIVERING ONE, and it has to be.
# This fixture called `(?&piece)` plainly until the addendum, back when every
# named group was injected flat; under the ruled model a plain call delivers
# NOTHING, so the plain form made this file assert an empty table. The plain
# call's own behaviour is covered by `deliver_forms.rxtin`, where it is one
# of four shapes over one definition.
target = user

pattern ^(?&d=piece)$
name user

pattern (?<kept>a)(b)(c)\2
name piece
export kept
